-- a binding claim transports along identity of molecules: if the two molecules are identical, a claim
-- about one is a claim about the other, with its event and its warrant carried along unchanged. This
-- is what the graph guarantees and what a digest cannot: the transport is along the path, so a
-- collision of digests licenses nothing (collision-not-injective), and a relation that does not
-- compose licenses nothing either (non-transitive-not-identity). Every inference the pharmacology
-- record makes from one molecule to another has to be one of these three, and only the first holds.
bind-transport : (b : BindClaim) → (N : Mol) → bind-mol b ≡ N → BindClaim
bind-transport b N p = (N , bind-prot b , bind-meas b)
